-* **PS1.** No part VM yet (CR10): the PS1 creator does not offer these rows (`LOOK_POOL_SAVED` 0). GBA / Dreamcast offer them.
+* **Age gate on a pool run.** `look_resolve_mask` drops a pool-run value whose `part_age_ok(PL_DEEP0 + f, v, stage)` is false
+  (the stage comes from the resident; a caller with no resident keeps the raw run), so a teen-only piercing never draws on a baby,
+  toddler or child, even from stale or foreign pool data (test `cr4_a7_a_teen_only_pool_run_does_not_resolve_on_a_minor`).
+* **PS1 (not in this tranche).** CR10 left 480 B of CREATOR's 21,504 B resident share. With A7 on, the PS1 EXE grew 1,376 B
+  (110,560 -> 109,184 B below the stack top): 444 B of `PartRef` rows (4 B a part), 48 B of lists, 36 B of set header, about 750 B
+  of painter hooks (`hand_acc`, `ph_face_acc`, neck, back, belt) and the age gate, 52 B of age rows and field tables. That is 896 B over
+  the share, and code cannot be trimmed by dropping parts. So the PS1 builds none of it: `DOOMO_ACC_DEEP` (`look_fields.h`) is 0
+  there (no painter hooks, no creator rows, no age gate), and `parts_build.py` sorts the `acc` set last in the registry and
+  `parts_index.c` / `parts_acc.c` leave it out of the PS1 build (`PS1_SKIP`); `ps1/tools/partsbin.py` follows the registry, so
+  PARTS.BIN holds no accessory scripts. The pool run, the save and the hash carry the ids on every platform: a GBA look with a mask
+  loads on the PS1 and shows without it. Measured: PS1 110,560 -> 110,464 B below the stack top (-96 B: the wider field tables).
+  PARTS.BIN carries the packed icons of all rows (one icon set, CR10): 145,408 -> 155,648 B of 184,320 B (+10,240 B for
+  icons the PS1 cannot show yet); room left 28,672 B. **To put A7 on the PS1 (A7-PS1):** about 1,380 B resident (the coordinator
+  releases the reserve), +5,500 B of scripts in PARTS.BIN (fits), flip `DOOMO_ACC_DEEP` and empty `PS1_SKIP`.
+* **Known: text fit.** Several A7 names are longer than the value column of the Outfit and Face rows ("Hoop Earr...", "Surgical
+  Mask") and the grid caption cuts "Wool Scarf - Cozy Hom" at 240x160. Names and layout are for CR-UI's TEXT FITS EVERYWHERE pass
+  (names are catalog data: shorten there).
+* **Review.** Sheets `interplay_back_0..2`, `interplay_mask_0..1` (header overprint fixed), `views_gloves`, `views_belt`, `slot_neck`,
+  `slot_face_pierce` were generated and looked at on the rebased tree: cartoon objects only, no nudity, nothing suggestive, no hate
+  symbols, no tobacco, vape or drug items. Runner script `creator_parts_acc.txt` (Dress-ups rows and Piercings; not run on the PS1).
 
